  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New undoable command `TurnFixture` (`crates/app/src/commands/fixture_turn.rs`). It turns one fixture about world X, Y or Z through the fixture origin. The write is a `MoveFixture`, so plate riders turn with the fixture.\n- Quarter turns write exact quaternion components (`settle_rot`). A turn that changes nothing (0 or 360 degrees) is refused. This obeys #2177.\n- A part or the stock that touched the fixture before the turn stays in position. The warning names each one (`fixture_clash::held_by`).\n- The turn does not make toolpaths stale. The post gate reads the turned fixture live. A turn into the tool path blocks the post with \"strikes a fixture\".\n- Fixtures page place draft: \"Place yaw\" is replaced by \"Tilt about X (roll)\", \"Tilt about Y (pitch)\" and \"Turn about Z (yaw)\". Six buttons \"Turn X+\" .. \"Turn Z-\" apply a quarter turn immediately. The row text shows roll and pitch when the fixture is not upright.\n- New MCP tool `turn_fixture` (`crates/app/src/mcp/fixture_turn_tools.rs`), with a row in the `camcraft-mcp` skill.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/2174-fixture-turns.md`.\n\nProcess change: yes (one row added to `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/app/tests/fixture_turn.rs`: `a_quarter_turn_about_each_axis_is_exact_and_undo_and_redo_restore_it`, `a_typed_angle_turns_by_it_and_undo_and_redo_restore_it`, `four_quarter_turns_are_the_exact_start_and_a_zero_turn_is_refused`, `a_fixture_turned_into_the_tools_path_blocks_the_post_without_a_regenerate`, `a_turned_fixture_names_the_stock_it_held_and_a_free_one_names_nothing`.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_fixture_turn.rs`: `turn_fixture_turns_by_a_quarter_undo_walks_it_back_and_bad_input_is_refused`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/fixture_rows.rs`: `the_place_draft_turns_a_fixture_by_a_quarter_about_each_axis` (labels, Button role, enabled state, inside the pane, the queued command, the exact result). `PLACE_FIELDS` now names the three angle fields.\n\n## Readings\n\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`): app suites ok (929 s). ui suites: one failure, `stock_fit_controls_follow_the_selected_shape`. This failure is known on main (#2170).\n- First ui run also failed `the_fixtures_page_keeps_every_input_named`: the taller place draft pushed \"Dowel pair\" off the 900 px harness. The harness in `fixtures_page.rs` is now 1100 px high. The rerun is green.\n- Clippy `-p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings`: clean.\n- No snapshot PNG changed. The UI assertions are in `fixture_rows.rs`, because `structural.rs` is over 400 lines.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No hand test in the live window. The screenshots come from the kittest harness render of the shipping shell with the GPU viewport, 1440x960.\n- A held part or stock does not follow the turn. This is a decision, not a gap (see the decision file).\n\n## Screenshots\n\nBefore (main): the place draft has one yaw field.\n![before](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/28f7cad4a1a680655914fe8759083b4bfd685fe7/issue-2174/before-fixtures.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter: three angles and six quarter-turn buttons.\n![after](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/28f7cad4a1a680655914fe8759083b4bfd685fe7/issue-2174/after-fixtures.png?raw=true)\n\nAfter \"Turn Y+\": the cube turns under the XY plane, the row shows pitch 90.\n![after turned](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/blob/28f7cad4a1a680655914fe8759083b4bfd685fe7/issue-2174/after-turned.png?raw=true)\n\nChangelog: Fixtures page: turn a fixture by quarter turns about X, Y or Z, or by typed roll, pitch and yaw angles; new MCP tool `turn_fixture`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2174\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
